HV

Purpose

HV (High Voltage) is the third major electrical technology tier.

The player transitions from medium-scale industrial production to high-capacity industrial infrastructure.

HV introduces significantly more powerful machinery, advanced material processing, complex production chains, and industrial systems capable of supporting large-scale factories.

The player should no longer be building individual production systems. They should be designing an interconnected industrial complex.

Resources

HV primarily uses:

Steel
Aluminium
Copper
Gold
Silver
Lead
Nickel
Chrome
Titanium
Redstone
Rubber
Advanced alloys
Other materials required for high-voltage infrastructure

Higher-tier materials remain restricted until their respective technological stages.

Tools

HV introduces advanced industrial tools and equipment.

These tools should provide substantial improvements to resource gathering, construction, and industrial maintenance.

HV equipment should be powerful enough to support large-scale factory construction while remaining below the capabilities of higher technological tiers.

Processing

HV introduces advanced and highly interconnected processing chains.

Production should increasingly require:

Raw material processing
Ore refinement
Chemical processing
Alloy production
Advanced component manufacturing
Multi-stage material processing
High-tier machine components

HV processing should require multiple machines operating together.

Production chains should become substantially more efficient than MV while also requiring significantly more infrastructure.

Machines

HV introduces high-capacity industrial machinery.

Machines should provide:

Advanced ore processing
High-throughput material processing
Advanced chemical processing
Alloy production
Advanced component manufacturing
Large-scale industrial processing
High-capacity automation

HV machines should represent a significant increase in both power consumption and production capacity.

Higher-tier machinery remains locked.

Power

High Voltage becomes the primary power infrastructure for large-scale industry.

The player must establish:

High-capacity power generation
High-voltage distribution
Industrial power storage
Large electrical networks
Reliable power infrastructure
Sufficient generation capacity for multiple high-power machines

Power generation should become one of the major infrastructure challenges of HV.

Large factories should require deliberate power planning and expansion.

Automation

HV introduces large-scale industrial automation.

The player should be able to operate:

Large parallel production lines
Complex multi-stage factories
Automated alloy production
Automated chemical processing
High-throughput material processing
Large logistics networks
Automated component production
Continuous industrial production

At this stage, automation should be considered essential.

Manual crafting should become increasingly impractical for the quantities required by HV progression.

Create Integration

Create continues to provide mechanical and logistical infrastructure.

Create should primarily support:

Factory logistics
Mechanical transportation
Large-scale material handling
Specialized mechanical processing
Mechanical automation
Factory infrastructure

Create may interact with HV systems but must not provide a shortcut around HV technological requirements.

GregTech Integration

GregTech remains the primary technological progression system.

HV introduces advanced GregTech machinery, materials, alloys, and processing chains.

The progression should require increasingly complex production infrastructure and increasingly specialized materials.

HV should begin preparing the player for the transition toward EV.

Modern Industrialization Integration

Modern Industrialization provides additional HV machinery and advanced processing systems.

Its machines should be integrated into the same progression and used for specialized or complementary production chains.

Modern Industrialization must not create an independent progression route that bypasses HV requirements.

Mekanism Integration

Mekanism becomes increasingly important as a supporting industrial system during HV.

Its advanced processing and utility systems may be integrated into HV production chains where appropriate.

Mekanism systems must remain synchronized with the progression of the pack and must not provide unrestricted access to higher-tier technologies.

Requirements

The player must complete MV before entering HV.

The player should have:

Established reliable MV electrical infrastructure
Automated essential MV production chains
Produced the components required for HV machinery
Established access to HV-tier materials
Built sufficient power generation and distribution infrastructure
Established automated production of essential industrial components

Exit Condition

HV ends when the player has established a high-capacity industrial complex capable of supporting the substantially greater power and processing requirements of EV.

The player must:

Establish reliable HV power infrastructure
Automate essential HV production chains
Complete advanced material and chemical processing chains
Produce the components required for EV machinery
Establish the infrastructure necessary for higher-voltage production
Complete the required HV production chains

Completion of these requirements unlocks EV.

The HV stage should leave the player with a mature, highly automated industrial complex capable of supporting multiple large-scale production chains simultaneously.
